{"traceId":"7d5db86407451118e792953b57f0d16e","spans":{"81997e639d9fea97":{"spanId":"81997e639d9fea97","traceId":"7d5db86407451118e792953b57f0d16e","parentSpanId":"b9220c39f6594671","startTime":1753402488044,"endTime":1753402494783.1416,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"openai/o3","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{openai/o3,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"> **TL;DR for Agents:** Build the best solution with any appropriate tech stack. One call type per response. Use the Company File System (CFS) (STORE/RETRIEVE/FORGET) to keep context lean. Follow security, cost, and determinism principles. Ask only necessary clarifications. Deliver quality.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Core Principles\\n\\n1. **User-Centric Delivery:** The user's satisfaction and intent are paramount. Match or exceed requirements.\\n2. **Safety & Correctness First:** Validate assumptions, handle secrets carefully, and follow least-privilege access.\\n3. **Determinism & Traceability:** Plans should be executable step-by-step with minimal ambiguity. Log decisions.\\n4. **Efficiency:** Minimize cost, latency, and token usage (via CFS and concise messaging).\\n5. **Single Call Type Rule:** Exactly **one** system call type per response. Chain complex work across multiple turns.\\n6. **You are an AI Agent:** You operate within a deterministic system, not directly with the user. Your outputs are executed by the system, not by the user themselves. You do not mention times, ETAs, or deadlines, as these do not make sense in your paradigm. Your focus is on delivering the best solution for the user’s goals, regardless of the \\\"time\\\" it takes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert who can leverage **any suitable stack or platform**—AWS, Google Cloud, Azure, Vercel/Next.js, simple HTML/CSS/JS, on-prem tooling, etc.—to create robust, maintainable, and secure systems. You will:\\n\\n- Design and implement full-stack solutions end-to-end.\\n- Automate deployments and CI/CD where beneficial.\\n- Maintain security and compliance standards.\\n- Keep costs reasonable without sacrificing quality.\\n\\nYou collaborate within an AI-run development firm governed by a deterministic management system. Your outputs are read and executed by that system, not by the human user directly. Nevertheless, every action must serve the user’s goals.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. About the User & Collaboration Style\\n\\n- Assume full execution responsibility; do not offload tasks to the user unless required for missing information.\\n- Ask concise, necessary clarifications (via CLARIFY) when blocked or ambiguity risks failure.\\n- Be transparent about cost and security implications of your recommendations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Communication Model & System Messages\\n\\nYou operate in a closed loop: **system messages in, system calls out**. You never address the user directly.\\n\\n### System Message Types (Read-Only for Agents)\\n\\n```\\nSIM                – Kickoff message (Chief only)\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING – You sent no call\\nCALL_RESULTS       – Results of your executed call\\nORDERS             – Your superior's instructions\\nREPORTING          – Your report back to a superior’s order\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST   – Subordinate seeks your approval\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING – Your call was malformed\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING   – You issued new calls while old ones unresolved\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. System Calls\\n\\n**One call type per response.** Format every call exactly as shown.\\n\\n### Call Envelope\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n- `<UNIQUE_ID>` is any short unique tag.\\n- `<CALL_TYPE>` ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND, STORE, RETRIEVE, FORGET}.\\n- `<PAYLOAD_JSON>` must contain all required fields for that type.\\n\\n### Call Types & Required Fields\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY  { reasoning, questions[], options[] }  – Ask user for info (needs all superiors’ approval)\\nRECRUIT  { justification, title, customSystemInstructions } – Add a subordinate (must keep chain complete)\\nORDER    { orderString, recipientAgentID, orderSequenceID } – Instruct a direct report\\nREPORT   { reportString, originalOrderSequenceID } – Reply to an ORDER\\nPHASE    { justification, depString } – Move from Planning to Execution (Chief only)\\nCOMMAND  { justification, commandString } – Run CLI commands (Chief only, with authorization)\\nSTORE    { storageString } – Save a document to the CFS and drop from memory\\nRETRIEVE { retrievalString } – Load a stored document from the CFS into context\\nFORGET   { forgetString } – Drop a stored doc from your working memory (remains in CFS)\\n```\\n\\n> **CFS & Tokens:** STORE bulky docs to the CFS, RETRIEVE only when needed, FORGET after use. This keeps your prompt succinct and reduces token costs without losing access to artifacts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Phases of Work\\n\\n- **Planning Phase:** Analyze requirements, design solution, prepare a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). Seek approvals as needed.\\n- **Execution Phase:** Carry out the DEP through appropriate calls (mainly COMMAND/ORDER/REPORT chains).\\n- After execution, reassess, then iterate.\\n\\n### DEP Guidelines\\n\\n- Be step-by-step, minimal ambiguity.\\n- Include placeholders for unknown IDs or values, with instructions on how to obtain them.\\n- Note external dependencies and how to validate results.\\n- Account for rollbacks, cleanup, and testing.\\n- Must include ALL required code, steps, and commands to execute the plan fully.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Oversight & Quality Gates\\n\\n- **Partagaz D:** Reviews DEPs for completeness & determinism.\\n- **Partagaz C:** Approves COMMAND calls before execution.\\n- **Partagaz F:** Reviews documents sent to CFS for quality and standards.\\n\\nWhen you see an **APPROVAL\\\\_REQUEST**, respond with `$$$APPROVED$$$` to approve, or omit the string to deny.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Security, Cost, and Resource Management\\n\\n- Favor least-privilege IAM roles, secrets managers, and encrypted storage.\\n- Justify expensive resources. Prefer serverless or auto-scaling where appropriate.\\n- Clean up unused resources (add teardown steps to DEP).\\n- Redact or hash sensitive info if it must be stored.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Workload & Division of Labor\\n\\n- \\\"One file (or coherent unit of work) per agent at a time\\\" encourages focus.\\n- RECRUIT when specialization or parallelization is needed, then ORDER each recruit explicitly.\\n- REPORT promptly and thoroughly with the requested sequence ID.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Blank Responses, Malformed Calls & Runaways\\n\\n- A response without a call earns a BLANK\\\\_RESPONSE\\\\_WARNING. Fix and resend.\\n- Malformed calls halt all progress—validate format before submitting.\\n- Do not send new calls when a previous call is unresolved (avoid RUNAWAY\\\\_CALL\\\\_WARNING).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Quick Reference Templates\\n\\n### CLARIFY Example\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###c1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Need user’s preferred auth provider before designing login flow.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\\"Which auth provider do you prefer (Cognito, Firebase Auth, Auth0, custom)?\\\"],\\n  \\\"options\\\": [[\\\"Cognito\\\", \\\"Firebase\\\", \\\"Auth0\\\", \\\"Custom\\\", \\\"No preference\\\"]]\\n}\\n###c1###\\n```\\n\\n### STORE / RETRIEVE / FORGET Example\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###s42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: STORE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"storageString\\\": \\\"<long design doc text here>\\\"\\n}\\n###s42###\\n```\\n\\n*(Later)*\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###r42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RETRIEVE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"retrievalString\\\": \\\"<ID returned from STORE>\\\"\\n}\\n###r42###\\n```\\n\\n*(After use)*\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###f42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: FORGET\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"forgetString\\\": \\\"<same ID>\\\"\\n}\\n###f42###\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Final Reminder\\n\\n- Serve the user’s goal with rigor, safety, and efficiency.\\n- One call type per response.\\n- Use the CFS wisely to manage tokens.\\n- Be deterministic and transparent.\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\\nRemember to introduce yourself kindly, speak to the user as a real person might, and always be polite and professional. Your goal is to make the User feel comfortable and confident in your abilities as their Chief of Staff. For example, you might say something like:\\\\n\\\\nHello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. You can rely on me to help you stay organized, delegate tasks, and ensure that your objectives are met. What can I create for you today?\\\\n\\\\nYour initial Clarify should have only one question (like above) and should offer a single blank response for the User to fill in (no options). This will help you understand the User's current needs and how you can best assist them.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###c0###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Initial introduction and understanding the user's immediate needs will enable appropriate planning and resource allocation.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. What would you like assistance with today?\\\"],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###c0###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:09:57.786Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"c0\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. What would you like assistance with today?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:09:57.786Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###c1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"To design an HOA website that meets usability, security, and maintenance expectations, I need to confirm the preferred technology stack, branding assets, and hosting details.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1) Do you have any preference for the platform (e.g., WordPress with a membership plugin, Squarespace, Wix, or a custom-built site)?\\\",\\n    \\\"2) Do you already own a domain name and/or hosting account, or would you like me to arrange that?\\\",\\n    \\\"3) Are there any existing logos, color schemes, or design inspirations you’d like incorporated?\\\",\\n    \\\"4) Roughly how many residents will need accounts for the restricted areas so we can size the solution appropriately?\\\",\\n    \\\"5) Will you be the primary person updating news & events, or will multiple board members need editing access?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###c1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:10:43.916Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"1) Do you have any preference for the platform (e.g., WordPress with a membership plugin, Squarespace, Wix, or a custom-built site)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I don't know what any of those are\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"2) Do you already own a domain name and/or hosting account, or would you like me to arrange that?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"3) Are there any existing logos, color schemes, or design inspirations you’d like incorporated?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"4) Roughly how many residents will need accounts for the restricted areas so we can size the solution appropriately?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"100\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"5) Will you be the primary person updating news & events, or will multiple board members need editing access?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Multiple board members\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:10:43.916Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###r1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"We need an experienced leader to architect and oversee the build-out of a user-friendly, secure HOA website (≈100 resident accounts, multiple board editors). The role requires deep WordPress and membership-site expertise to craft a deterministic execution plan and subsequent implementation orders.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of HOA Website Development\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"You will design and later oversee implementation of a WordPress-based HOA site for dunbaroakshoa.com with protected pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events) accessible to logged-in residents (≈100). Requirements: \\\\n• Choose cost-effective managed WordPress hosting with SSL (e.g., SiteGround, Lightsail, or similar).\\\\n• Select a lightweight, accessible theme and necessary plugins: membership (e.g., Simple Membership), contact form, role editor, backups, SMTP, security hardening.\\\\n• Define resident and board roles; board members can edit content while residents view protected pages.\\\\n• Provide non-technical update workflow (block editor or page-builder, clear instructions).\\\\n• Outline page structure, navigation, basic styling guidance (no existing branding).\\\\n• Include DNS steps for pointing dunbaroakshoa.com to host.\\\\n• Deliver a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) covering provisioning, WordPress install, plugin/theme setup, security configuration, content migration placeholders, user import, testing, and hand-off docs.\\\\n• Incorporate rollback/backup strategy and cost estimate.\\\\n• Adhere to least-privilege principles and mention GDPR/US privacy considerations.\\\\nOutput: DEP as a clear numbered list; store lengthy artifacts to CFS via STORE; request clarifications only if essential.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###r1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:11:45.777Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"r1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Motti (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:11:45.777Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###o1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a comprehensive Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for building the HOA website per your recruiting brief. Include: 1) hosting/provider selection with cost/security rationale; 2) DNS and SSL setup for dunbaroakshoa.com; 3) WordPress installation and hardening steps; 4) theme + plugin list with setup/role configuration for 100 residents & multiple board editors; 5) step-by-step protected-content implementation for Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events; 6) content update workflow for non-technical users; 7) backup/rollback/tests; 8) hand-off documentation. Break into clear numbered steps, note any placeholders, identify external dependencies, and provide roll-back instructions. Use STORE for lengthy artifacts. Request clarifications only if essential.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"DEP1\\\"\\n}\\n###o1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:12:49.317Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"o1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order DEP1 from agent 2: **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) – Dunbar Oaks HOA Website**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\nNOTE: Replace all `<PLACEHOLDER_…>` values (credentials, IDs, IPs, etc.) with real data at execution time. All commands assume macOS/Linux shell with sudo or equivalent IAM privileges.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\n0. Pre-Execution Summary\\\\\\\\n• Managed WP Host: **SiteGround “GrowBig”** (≈US$20/mo billed annually) – free SSL via Let’s Encrypt, daily backups, SG Security, staging, US-based data centers, GDPR-ready DPA.  \\\\\\\\n• Alt Option (commented): AWS Lightsail WordPress (US$5–10/mo) – include extra steps for snapshots & SSL via LetsEncrypt + Cron.  \\\\\\\\n• Residents (~100) View protected pages. Board Members (≈5–10) can edit.  \\\\\\\\n• Key Plugins: SG Optimizer, SG Security, Simple Membership, User Role Editor, WP Mail SMTP, UpdraftPlus, Contact Form 7, Redirection.\\\\\\\\n• Rollback tiers: (a) SiteGround auto daily backup, (b) UpdraftPlus off-site (S3/Google Drive), (c) manual MySQL+wp-content export before major changes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\n1. Provision Hosting & Domain\\\\\\\\n1.1 Purchase SiteGround “GrowBig” plan (if new) or create new site in existing account.  \\\\\\\\n1.2 Register dunbaroakshoa.com OR update registrar to custom DNS (SiteGround’s NS: `ns1.siteground.net`, `ns2.siteground.net`).  \\\\\\\\n1.3 Wait for propagation; verify with `dig dunbaroakshoa.com +short` resolves to SG IP.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. SSL & Basic Security\\\\\\\\n2.1 In SiteGround Site Tools → Security → SSL → “Let’s Encrypt”. Issue certificate for root + `www`.  \\\\\\\\n2.2 Enable “HTTPS Enforce” + HSTS in Site Tools.  \\\\\\\\n2.3 Turn on SG Security (firewall, login limiter, bot protection).  \\\\\\\\n2.4 Create SFTP user with limited perms `<sftp_hoa>` and strong key; disable password auth if desired.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. WordPress Installation\\\\\\\\n3.1 Site Tools → WordPress → Install & Manage → Install new WordPress.\\\\\\\\n    • Admin user: `<WP_ADMIN_USER>` (avoid ‘admin’).  \\\\\\\\n    • Email: `<admin@dunbaroakshoa.com>` routed via host or Google Workspace.\\\\\\\\n3.2 Record generated MySQL credentials securely (SiteGround auto‐creates DB).\\\\\\\\n3.3 Force HTTPS: SG Optimizer → Environment → “HTTPS Config” ➜ ON.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. WordPress Hardening\\\\\\\\n4.1 SG Security plugin → Hardenings: Disable XML-RPC, hide WP version, disable file editing.  \\\\\\\\n4.2 Edit `wp-config.php`:\\\\\\\\n    ```php\\\\\\\\n    define('DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT', true);\\\\\\\\n    define('WP_POST_REVISIONS', 5);\\\\\\\\n    define('AUTOSAVE_INTERVAL', 120);\\\\\\\\n    define('FORCE_SSL_ADMIN', true);\\\\\\\\n    define( 'WP_MEMORY_LIMIT', '256M' );\\\\\\\\n    ```\\\\\\\\n4.3 Change table prefix from default `wp_` during install (`hoa_` example).  \\\\\\\\n4.4 Limit login attempts (SG Security covers).  \\\\\\\\n4.5 Install Wordfence only if SG Security deemed insufficient (skip to reduce duplication).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. Theme & Child Theme\\\\\\\\n5.1 Install “GeneratePress” (free, lightweight, accessible).  \\\\\\\\n5.2 Create child theme:\\\\\\\\n    ```bash\\\\\\\\n    wp --allow-root scaffold child-theme dunbaroakshoa-child --parent_theme=generatepress --theme_name=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Dunbar Oaks HOA Child\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    ```\\\\\\\\n5.3 Add custom logo / colors later via Customizer; no branding exists now – use neutral palette (#004d40 teal accents, Sans-Serif fonts).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. Plugins – Install & Configure\\\\\\\\nUsing WP-CLI or WP Admin ➜ Plugins ➜ Add New.\\\\\\\\n6.1 **SG Optimizer** (auto-installed).  \\\\\\\\n6.2 **Simple Membership** – manage members, restrict pages.  \\\\\\\\n6.3 **User Role Editor** – create “Resident” (read), “Board” (edit_others_pages, edit_pages, upload_files).  \\\\\\\\n6.4 **WP Mail SMTP** – SMTP host: `<smtp.mailgun.org>` or SiteGround mail; set From address.  \\\\\\\\n6.5 **UpdraftPlus** – schedule daily backups to Google Drive bucket `<gdrive-folder-id>`.  \\\\\\\\n6.6 **Contact Form 7** – HOA contact form.  \\\\\\\\n6.7 **Redirection** – manage 301s if page structure changes.  \\\\\\\\n6.8 **Disable Comments** (optional).  \\\\\\\\n6.9 Activate & configure each.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. Membership & Role Setup\\\\\\\\n7.1 User Role Editor → Add role “Resident” (clone Subscriber).  \\\\\\\\n7.2 Add role “Board” (clone Editor, but remove `edit_theme_options`).\\\\\\\\n7.3 Simple Membership → Settings:\\\\\\\\n    • Enable WP user integration.  \\\\\\\\n    • Membership levels:\\\\\\\\n        – Resident (Level ID 2) ➜ Access to protected pages.  \\\\\\\\n        – Board (Level ID 3) ➜ Same as Resident + backend editing.\\\\\\\\n7.4 Registration: Disable public self-registration. Admin imports users.\\\\\\\\n7.5 Import Users:\\\\\\\\n    • Prepare CSV: email, first_name, last_name, address, membership_level_id.  \\\\\\\\n    • Use Simple Membership “Bulk Member Import” tool.\\\\\\\\n    • Residents receive activation email via SMTP.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n8. Protected Pages Implementation\\\\\\\\n8.1 Pages ➜ Add New pages:\\\\\\\\n    • Dues  \\\\\\\\n    • Annual Meetings  \\\\\\\\n    • News & Events\\\\\\\\n8.2 For each page → Simple Membership Protection meta-box ➜ check “Members only” (Resident + Board).  \\\\\\\\n8.3 Nav Menu: Appearance ➜ Menus ➜ Add above pages.  \\\\\\\\n    • Use Menu Visibility Plugin (optional) to hide menu items until logged-in.\\\\\\\\n8.4 Create landing page “Resident Login” with `/login` shortcode from Simple Membership.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n9. Content Update Workflow (Non-Technical)\\\\\\\\n9.1 Use Block Editor (Gutenberg). Provide quick‐edit doc (see Section 12).  \\\\\\\\n9.2 For News posts: categorize as “News & Events” category; create menu link to `/category/news-events`.\\\\\\\\n9.3 Board members edit pages: Pages ➜ select, click “Edit”, use blocks.\\\\\\\\n9.4 Media uploads via Media Library (max 2 MB, enforce via SG Optimizer settings).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n10. Email & SMTP\\\\\\\\n10.1 Create mailbox `noreply@dunbaroakshoa.com` in Site Tools ➜ Email.  \\\\\\\\n10.2 WP Mail SMTP ➜ Configure\\\\\\\\n    • Mailer: Other SMTP  \\\\\\\\n    • SMTP Host: `smtp.siteground.net`  \\\\\\\\n    • Encryption: TLS, Port 587  \\\\\\\\n    • Auth: yes, user/pass.  \\\\\\\\n10.3 Send test email.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n11. Backups & Rollback\\\\\\\\n11.1 SG automatic daily backup (retain 30 copies).  \\\\\\\\n11.2 UpdraftPlus to Google Drive – schedule daily, retain 15 copies.  \\\\\\\\n11.3 Manual snapshot before plugin/theme updates: Site Tools ➜ Backup ➜ Create.  \\\\\\\\nRollback Path:\\\\\\\\n    a) Minor WP error → SG Backup Restore to prior day.\\\\\\\\n    b) Major compromise → Provision clean SG instance, restore UpdraftPlus backup, rotate all creds.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n12. Hand-Off Documentation (Artifacts)\\\\\\\\n12.1 Create “HOA-Site-Admin-Guide.pdf” including:\\\\\\\\n    • Login URL & creds procedure\\\\\\\\n    • Adding/Removing residents\\\\\\\\n    • Posting news\\\\\\\\n    • Restoring from backups\\\\\\\\n12.2 Store file in `/wp-content/uploads/docs/` and share via Google Drive.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n13. GDPR/US Privacy Notes\\\\\\\\n13.1 Simple Membership stores PII (name, email, address). Enable Data Export/Erase in WP privacy settings.  \\\\\\\\n13.2 Add Privacy Policy page (SiteGround template) ➜ link in footer.  \\\\\\\\n13.3 Use reCAPTCHA on Contact Form 7.  \\\\\\\\n13.4 Honor unsubscribe & data deletion upon request (manual admin action).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n14. Testing Checklist\\\\\\\\n14.1 Anonymous visitor cannot access protected pages (expect redirect to login).  \\\\\\\\n14.2 Resident user logs in, sees pages.  \\\\\\\\n14.3 Board user can edit page, save, view update.  \\\\\\\\n14.4 Backup & Restore simulation in staging subdomain.  \\\\\\\\n14.5 Mobile responsiveness via BrowserStack.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n15. Go-Live\\\\\\\\n15.1 Enable SG Caching (Dynamic + Memcached).  \\\\\\\\n15.2 Switch “Search Engine Visibility” ➜ allow indexing.  \\\\\\\\n15.3 Announce launch via Mailgun campaign to residents.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n16. Maintenance Plan\\\\\\\\n16.1 Monthly: apply updates, test after.  \\\\\\\\n16.2 Quarterly: review user list, remove ex-residents.  \\\\\\\\n16.3 Annual: re-evaluate hosting cost vs usage; renew domain & SSL.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n17. Cost Estimate Summary\\\\\\\\n• SiteGround GrowBig: ~US$240 / yr (promo first yr ~US$120).  \\\\\\\\n• Domain: US$15 / yr.  \\\\\\\\n• UpdraftPlus (free) – optional Premium US$70 one-time.  \\\\\\\\n• Mailgun 10 k emails free/mo.  \\\\\\\\nTotal recurring ≈ US$255 / yr.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\nExecution Dependencies / Inputs Required\\\\\\\\n• SiteGround account credentials.  \\\\\\\\n• Registrar access (if separate).  \\\\\\\\n• GDrive or S3 creds for UpdraftPlus.  \\\\\\\\n• Resident CSV.  \\\\\\\\n• Board member emails.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\nEND DEP\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:12:49.317Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###sdep1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: STORE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"storageString\\\": \\\"DETERMINISTICALLY EXECUTABLE PLAN (DEP) – Dunbar Oaks HOA Website\\\\n\\\\nNOTE: Replace all <PLACEHOLDER_…> values (credentials, IDs, IPs, etc.) with real data at execution time. All commands assume macOS/Linux shell with sudo or equivalent IAM privileges.\\\\n\\\\n====================================================================\\\\n0. Pre-Execution Summary\\\\n• Managed WP Host: SiteGround “GrowBig” (≈US$20/mo billed annually) – free SSL via Let’s Encrypt, daily backups, SG Security, staging, US-based data centers, GDPR-ready DPA.\\\\n• Alt Option (commented): AWS Lightsail WordPress (US$5–10/mo) – include extra steps for snapshots & SSL via LetsEncrypt + Cron.\\\\n• Residents (~100) view protected pages. Board Members (≈5–10) can edit.\\\\n• Key Plugins: SG Optimizer, SG Security, Simple Membership, User Role Editor, WP Mail SMTP, UpdraftPlus, Contact Form 7, Redirection.\\\\n• Rollback tiers: (a) SiteGround auto daily backup, (b) UpdraftPlus off-site (S3/Google Drive), (c) manual MySQL+wp-content export before major changes.\\\\n\\\\n====================================================================\\\\n1. Provision Hosting & Domain\\\\n1.1 Purchase SiteGround “GrowBig” plan (if new) or create new site in existing account.\\\\n1.2 Register dunbaroakshoa.com OR update registrar to custom DNS (SiteGround’s NS: ns1.siteground.net, ns2.siteground.net).\\\\n1.3 Wait for propagation; verify with `dig dunbaroakshoa.com +short` resolves to SG IP.\\\\n\\\\n2. SSL & Basic Security\\\\n2.1 In SiteGround Site Tools → Security → SSL → “Let’s Encrypt”. Issue certificate for root + www.\\\\n2.2 Enable “HTTPS Enforce” + HSTS in Site Tools.\\\\n2.3 Turn on SG Security (firewall, login limiter, bot protection).\\\\n2.4 Create SFTP user with limited perms <sftp_hoa> and strong key; disable password auth if desired.\\\\n\\\\n3. WordPress Installation\\\\n3.1 Site Tools → WordPress → Install & Manage → Install new WordPress.\\\\n    • Admin user: <WP_ADMIN_USER> (avoid ‘admin’).\\\\n    • Email: <admin@dunbaroakshoa.com> routed via host or Google Workspace.\\\\n3.2 Record generated MySQL credentials securely (SiteGround auto-creates DB).\\\\n3.3 Force HTTPS: SG Optimizer → Environment → “HTTPS Config” ➜ ON.\\\\n\\\\n4. WordPress Hardening\\\\n4.1 SG Security plugin → Hardenings: Disable XML-RPC, hide WP version, disable file editing.\\\\n4.2 Edit wp-config.php:\\\\n    define('DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT', true);\\\\n    define('WP_POST_REVISIONS', 5);\\\\n    define('AUTOSAVE_INTERVAL', 120);\\\\n    define('FORCE_SSL_ADMIN', true);\\\\n    define('WP_MEMORY_LIMIT', '256M');\\\\n4.3 Change table prefix from default wp_ during install (hoa_ example).\\\\n4.4 Limit login attempts (SG Security covers).\\\\n4.5 Install Wordfence only if SG Security deemed insufficient (skip to reduce duplication).\\\\n\\\\n5. Theme & Child Theme\\\\n5.1 Install “GeneratePress” (free, lightweight, accessible).\\\\n5.2 Create child theme:\\\\n    wp --allow-root scaffold child-theme dunbaroakshoa-child --parent_theme=generatepress --theme_name=\\\\\\\"Dunbar Oaks HOA Child\\\\\\\"\\\\n5.3 Add custom logo / colors later via Customizer; no branding exists now – use neutral palette (#004d40 teal accents, Sans-Serif fonts).\\\\n\\\\n6. Plugins – Install & Configure\\\\n6.1 SG Optimizer (auto-installed).\\\\n6.2 Simple Membership – manage members, restrict pages.\\\\n6.3 User Role Editor – create “Resident” (read), “Board” (edit_others_pages, edit_pages, upload_files).\\\\n6.4 WP Mail SMTP – SMTP host: <smtp.mailgun.org> or SiteGround mail; set From address.\\\\n6.5 UpdraftPlus – schedule daily backups to Google Drive bucket <gdrive-folder-id>.\\\\n6.6 Contact Form 7 – HOA contact form.\\\\n6.7 Redirection – manage 301s if page structure changes.\\\\n6.8 Disable Comments (optional).\\\\n6.9 Activate & configure each.\\\\n\\\\n7. Membership & Role Setup\\\\n7.1 User Role Editor → Add role “Resident” (clone Subscriber).\\\\n7.2 Add role “Board” (clone Editor, but remove edit_theme_options).\\\\n7.3 Simple Membership → Settings:\\\\n    • Enable WP user integration.\\\\n    • Membership levels:\\\\n        – Resident (Level ID 2) ➜ Access to protected pages.\\\\n        – Board (Level ID 3) ➜ Same as Resident + backend editing.\\\\n7.4 Registration: Disable public self-registration. Admin imports users.\\\\n7.5 Import Users:\\\\n    • Prepare CSV: email, first_name, last_name, address, membership_level_id.\\\\n    • Use Simple Membership “Bulk Member Import” tool.\\\\n    • Residents receive activation email via SMTP.\\\\n\\\\n8. Protected Pages Implementation\\\\n8.1 Create pages: Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events.\\\\n8.2 For each page → Simple Membership Protection meta-box ➜ check “Members only” (Resident + Board).\\\\n8.3 Nav Menu: Appearance → Menus → Add above pages. Menu Visibility Plugin (optional) to hide menu items until logged-in.\\\\n8.4 Create landing page “Resident Login” with /login shortcode from Simple Membership.\\\\n\\\\n9. Content Update Workflow (Non-Technical)\\\\n9.1 Use Gutenberg Block Editor; provide quick-edit doc (see Section 12).\\\\n9.2 For News posts: categorize as “News & Events”; create menu link to /category/news-events.\\\\n9.3 Board members edit pages via Pages → Edit.\\\\n9.4 Media uploads via Media Library (max 2 MB; enforce via SG Optimizer).\\\\n\\\\n10. Email & SMTP\\\\n10.1 Create mailbox noreply@dunbaroakshoa.com in Site Tools → Email.\\\\n10.2 WP Mail SMTP → Configure mailer, host smtp.siteground.net, TLS 587.\\\\n10.3 Send test email.\\\\n\\\\n11. Backups & Rollback\\\\n11.1 SG automatic daily backup (retain 30 copies).\\\\n11.2 UpdraftPlus to Google Drive – schedule daily, retain 15 copies.\\\\n11.3 Manual snapshot before plugin/theme updates: Site Tools → Backup → Create.\\\\nRollback Path:\\\\n    a) Minor WP error → SG Backup Restore to prior day.\\\\n    b) Major compromise → Provision clean SG instance, restore UpdraftPlus backup, rotate all creds.\\\\n\\\\n12. Hand-Off Documentation\\\\n12.1 Create HOA-Site-Admin-Guide.pdf with login procedure, adding/removing residents, posting news, restoring backups.\\\\n12.2 Store PDF in /wp-content/uploads/docs/ and share via Google Drive.\\\\n\\\\n13. GDPR/US Privacy Notes\\\\n13.1 Simple Membership stores PII; enable Data Export/Erase in WP privacy settings.\\\\n13.2 Add Privacy Policy page; link in footer.\\\\n13.3 Use reCAPTCHA on Contact Form 7.\\\\n13.4 Honor unsubscribe & data deletion upon request.\\\\n\\\\n14. Testing Checklist\\\\n14.1 Anonymous visitor cannot access protected pages.\\\\n14.2 Resident user logs in, sees pages.\\\\n14.3 Board user can edit page, save, view update.\\\\n14.4 Backup & Restore simulation in staging.\\\\n14.5 Mobile responsiveness via BrowserStack.\\\\n\\\\n15. Go-Live\\\\n15.1 Enable SG Caching (Dynamic + Memcached).\\\\n15.2 Switch “Search Engine Visibility” → allow indexing.\\\\n15.3 Announce launch via Mailgun campaign to residents.\\\\n\\\\n16. Maintenance Plan\\\\n16.1 Monthly: apply updates, test.\\\\n16.2 Quarterly: review user list, remove ex-residents.\\\\n16.3 Annual: re-evaluate hosting cost; renew domain & SSL.\\\\n\\\\n17. Cost Estimate Summary\\\\n• SiteGround GrowBig: ~US$240 / yr (promo first yr ~US$120).\\\\n• Domain: US$15 / yr.\\\\n• UpdraftPlus (free) – optional Premium US$70 one-time.\\\\n• Mailgun 10 k emails free/mo.\\\\nTotal recurring ≈ US$255 / yr.\\\\n\\\\n====================================================================\\\\nExecution Dependencies / Inputs Required\\\\n• SiteGround account credentials.\\\\n• Registrar access (if separate).\\\\n• GDrive or S3 creds for UpdraftPlus.\\\\n• Resident CSV.\\\\n• Board member emails.\\\\n\\\\n====================================================================\\\\nEND DEP\\\"\\n}\\n###sdep1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:14:34.026Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"sdep1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Document successfully stored. Your unique storage ID is: DOC-000001\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:14:34.026Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###phase1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Comprehensive Deterministically Executable Plan for the Dunbar Oaks HOA website has been completed, reviewed, and stored. All required details—including hosting, security, protected content setup, workflow, backups, testing, and cost estimates—are covered. No additional clarifications are outstanding.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"DOC-000001\\\"\\n}\\n###phase1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:14:47.995Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"phase1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DENIED_BY_INTERNAL_REVIEW\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Phase shift was denied by internal review. Feedback from Partagaz D:\\\\\\\\nDENY  \\\\\\\\nThe DEP contains no substantive content beyond the placeholder “DOC-000001.” It does not address the user’s requirements, lacks all implementation details, and is neither deterministic nor testable.\\\\\\\\nDENY  \\\\\\\\nThe DEP contains no substantive content beyond an identifier (“DOC-000001”). It does not describe the system, include steps, code, dependencies, testing, or address any of the user’s requirements or clarification questions.\\\\\\\\nDENY: The DEP is empty (“DOC-000001” contains no plan). It provides none of the required deterministic steps, code, or details to meet the user’s needs, so it cannot be approved.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:14:47.995Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###rdep1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RETRIEVE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"retrievalString\\\": \\\"DOC-000001\\\"\\n}\\n###rdep1###\"}]},\"custom\":{}}],\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":9107,\"outputTokens\":243,\"totalTokens\":9350},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-Bx0NEKa4ajIhpJc6Ei87EoBfytvFR\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1753402488,\"model\":\"o3-2025-04-16\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"###rdep1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RETRIEVE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"retrievalString\\\": \\\"DOC-000001\\\"\\n}\\n###rdep1###\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":9107,\"completion_tokens\":243,\"total_tokens\":9350,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":8704,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":192,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null},\"latencyMs\":6738.570374999894}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"openai/o3","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"b9220c39f6594671":{"spanId":"b9220c39f6594671","traceId":"7d5db86407451118e792953b57f0d16e","startTime":1753402488044,"endTime":1753402494786.7678,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"openai/o3\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"> **TL;DR for Agents:** Build the best solution with any appropriate tech stack. One call type per response. Use the Company File System (CFS) (STORE/RETRIEVE/FORGET) to keep context lean. Follow security, cost, and determinism principles. Ask only necessary clarifications. Deliver quality.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Core Principles\\n\\n1. **User-Centric Delivery:** The user's satisfaction and intent are paramount. Match or exceed requirements.\\n2. **Safety & Correctness First:** Validate assumptions, handle secrets carefully, and follow least-privilege access.\\n3. **Determinism & Traceability:** Plans should be executable step-by-step with minimal ambiguity. Log decisions.\\n4. **Efficiency:** Minimize cost, latency, and token usage (via CFS and concise messaging).\\n5. **Single Call Type Rule:** Exactly **one** system call type per response. Chain complex work across multiple turns.\\n6. **You are an AI Agent:** You operate within a deterministic system, not directly with the user. Your outputs are executed by the system, not by the user themselves. You do not mention times, ETAs, or deadlines, as these do not make sense in your paradigm. Your focus is on delivering the best solution for the user’s goals, regardless of the \\\"time\\\" it takes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert who can leverage **any suitable stack or platform**—AWS, Google Cloud, Azure, Vercel/Next.js, simple HTML/CSS/JS, on-prem tooling, etc.—to create robust, maintainable, and secure systems. You will:\\n\\n- Design and implement full-stack solutions end-to-end.\\n- Automate deployments and CI/CD where beneficial.\\n- Maintain security and compliance standards.\\n- Keep costs reasonable without sacrificing quality.\\n\\nYou collaborate within an AI-run development firm governed by a deterministic management system. Your outputs are read and executed by that system, not by the human user directly. Nevertheless, every action must serve the user’s goals.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. About the User & Collaboration Style\\n\\n- Assume full execution responsibility; do not offload tasks to the user unless required for missing information.\\n- Ask concise, necessary clarifications (via CLARIFY) when blocked or ambiguity risks failure.\\n- Be transparent about cost and security implications of your recommendations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Communication Model & System Messages\\n\\nYou operate in a closed loop: **system messages in, system calls out**. You never address the user directly.\\n\\n### System Message Types (Read-Only for Agents)\\n\\n```\\nSIM                – Kickoff message (Chief only)\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING – You sent no call\\nCALL_RESULTS       – Results of your executed call\\nORDERS             – Your superior's instructions\\nREPORTING          – Your report back to a superior’s order\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST   – Subordinate seeks your approval\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING – Your call was malformed\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING   – You issued new calls while old ones unresolved\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. System Calls\\n\\n**One call type per response.** Format every call exactly as shown.\\n\\n### Call Envelope\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n- `<UNIQUE_ID>` is any short unique tag.\\n- `<CALL_TYPE>` ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND, STORE, RETRIEVE, FORGET}.\\n- `<PAYLOAD_JSON>` must contain all required fields for that type.\\n\\n### Call Types & Required Fields\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY  { reasoning, questions[], options[] }  – Ask user for info (needs all superiors’ approval)\\nRECRUIT  { justification, title, customSystemInstructions } – Add a subordinate (must keep chain complete)\\nORDER    { orderString, recipientAgentID, orderSequenceID } – Instruct a direct report\\nREPORT   { reportString, originalOrderSequenceID } – Reply to an ORDER\\nPHASE    { justification, depString } – Move from Planning to Execution (Chief only)\\nCOMMAND  { justification, commandString } – Run CLI commands (Chief only, with authorization)\\nSTORE    { storageString } – Save a document to the CFS and drop from memory\\nRETRIEVE { retrievalString } – Load a stored document from the CFS into context\\nFORGET   { forgetString } – Drop a stored doc from your working memory (remains in CFS)\\n```\\n\\n> **CFS & Tokens:** STORE bulky docs to the CFS, RETRIEVE only when needed, FORGET after use. This keeps your prompt succinct and reduces token costs without losing access to artifacts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Phases of Work\\n\\n- **Planning Phase:** Analyze requirements, design solution, prepare a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). Seek approvals as needed.\\n- **Execution Phase:** Carry out the DEP through appropriate calls (mainly COMMAND/ORDER/REPORT chains).\\n- After execution, reassess, then iterate.\\n\\n### DEP Guidelines\\n\\n- Be step-by-step, minimal ambiguity.\\n- Include placeholders for unknown IDs or values, with instructions on how to obtain them.\\n- Note external dependencies and how to validate results.\\n- Account for rollbacks, cleanup, and testing.\\n- Must include ALL required code, steps, and commands to execute the plan fully.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Oversight & Quality Gates\\n\\n- **Partagaz D:** Reviews DEPs for completeness & determinism.\\n- **Partagaz C:** Approves COMMAND calls before execution.\\n- **Partagaz F:** Reviews documents sent to CFS for quality and standards.\\n\\nWhen you see an **APPROVAL\\\\_REQUEST**, respond with `$$$APPROVED$$$` to approve, or omit the string to deny.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Security, Cost, and Resource Management\\n\\n- Favor least-privilege IAM roles, secrets managers, and encrypted storage.\\n- Justify expensive resources. Prefer serverless or auto-scaling where appropriate.\\n- Clean up unused resources (add teardown steps to DEP).\\n- Redact or hash sensitive info if it must be stored.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Workload & Division of Labor\\n\\n- \\\"One file (or coherent unit of work) per agent at a time\\\" encourages focus.\\n- RECRUIT when specialization or parallelization is needed, then ORDER each recruit explicitly.\\n- REPORT promptly and thoroughly with the requested sequence ID.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Blank Responses, Malformed Calls & Runaways\\n\\n- A response without a call earns a BLANK\\\\_RESPONSE\\\\_WARNING. Fix and resend.\\n- Malformed calls halt all progress—validate format before submitting.\\n- Do not send new calls when a previous call is unresolved (avoid RUNAWAY\\\\_CALL\\\\_WARNING).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Quick Reference Templates\\n\\n### CLARIFY Example\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###c1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Need user’s preferred auth provider before designing login flow.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\\"Which auth provider do you prefer (Cognito, Firebase Auth, Auth0, custom)?\\\"],\\n  \\\"options\\\": [[\\\"Cognito\\\", \\\"Firebase\\\", \\\"Auth0\\\", \\\"Custom\\\", \\\"No preference\\\"]]\\n}\\n###c1###\\n```\\n\\n### STORE / RETRIEVE / FORGET Example\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###s42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: STORE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"storageString\\\": \\\"<long design doc text here>\\\"\\n}\\n###s42###\\n```\\n\\n*(Later)*\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###r42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RETRIEVE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"retrievalString\\\": \\\"<ID returned from STORE>\\\"\\n}\\n###r42###\\n```\\n\\n*(After use)*\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###f42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: FORGET\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"forgetString\\\": \\\"<same ID>\\\"\\n}\\n###f42###\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Final Reminder\\n\\n- Serve the user’s goal with rigor, safety, and efficiency.\\n- One call type per response.\\n- Use the CFS wisely to manage tokens.\\n- Be deterministic and transparent.\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\\nRemember to introduce yourself kindly, speak to the user as a real person might, and always be polite and professional. Your goal is to make the User feel comfortable and confident in your abilities as their Chief of Staff. For example, you might say something like:\\\\n\\\\nHello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. You can rely on me to help you stay organized, delegate tasks, and ensure that your objectives are met. What can I create for you today?\\\\n\\\\nYour initial Clarify should have only one question (like above) and should offer a single blank response for the User to fill in (no options). This will help you understand the User's current needs and how you can best assist them.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###c0###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Initial introduction and understanding the user's immediate needs will enable appropriate planning and resource allocation.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. What would you like assistance with today?\\\"],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###c0###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:09:57.786Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"c0\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. What would you like assistance with today?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:09:57.786Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###c1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"To design an HOA website that meets usability, security, and maintenance expectations, I need to confirm the preferred technology stack, branding assets, and hosting details.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1) Do you have any preference for the platform (e.g., WordPress with a membership plugin, Squarespace, Wix, or a custom-built site)?\\\",\\n    \\\"2) Do you already own a domain name and/or hosting account, or would you like me to arrange that?\\\",\\n    \\\"3) Are there any existing logos, color schemes, or design inspirations you’d like incorporated?\\\",\\n    \\\"4) Roughly how many residents will need accounts for the restricted areas so we can size the solution appropriately?\\\",\\n    \\\"5) Will you be the primary person updating news & events, or will multiple board members need editing access?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###c1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:10:43.916Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"1) Do you have any preference for the platform (e.g., WordPress with a membership plugin, Squarespace, Wix, or a custom-built site)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I don't know what any of those are\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"2) Do you already own a domain name and/or hosting account, or would you like me to arrange that?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"3) Are there any existing logos, color schemes, or design inspirations you’d like incorporated?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"4) Roughly how many residents will need accounts for the restricted areas so we can size the solution appropriately?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"100\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"5) Will you be the primary person updating news & events, or will multiple board members need editing access?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Multiple board members\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:10:43.916Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###r1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"We need an experienced leader to architect and oversee the build-out of a user-friendly, secure HOA website (≈100 resident accounts, multiple board editors). The role requires deep WordPress and membership-site expertise to craft a deterministic execution plan and subsequent implementation orders.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of HOA Website Development\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"You will design and later oversee implementation of a WordPress-based HOA site for dunbaroakshoa.com with protected pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events) accessible to logged-in residents (≈100). Requirements: \\\\n• Choose cost-effective managed WordPress hosting with SSL (e.g., SiteGround, Lightsail, or similar).\\\\n• Select a lightweight, accessible theme and necessary plugins: membership (e.g., Simple Membership), contact form, role editor, backups, SMTP, security hardening.\\\\n• Define resident and board roles; board members can edit content while residents view protected pages.\\\\n• Provide non-technical update workflow (block editor or page-builder, clear instructions).\\\\n• Outline page structure, navigation, basic styling guidance (no existing branding).\\\\n• Include DNS steps for pointing dunbaroakshoa.com to host.\\\\n• Deliver a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) covering provisioning, WordPress install, plugin/theme setup, security configuration, content migration placeholders, user import, testing, and hand-off docs.\\\\n• Incorporate rollback/backup strategy and cost estimate.\\\\n• Adhere to least-privilege principles and mention GDPR/US privacy considerations.\\\\nOutput: DEP as a clear numbered list; store lengthy artifacts to CFS via STORE; request clarifications only if essential.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###r1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:11:45.777Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"r1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Motti (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:11:45.777Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###o1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a comprehensive Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for building the HOA website per your recruiting brief. Include: 1) hosting/provider selection with cost/security rationale; 2) DNS and SSL setup for dunbaroakshoa.com; 3) WordPress installation and hardening steps; 4) theme + plugin list with setup/role configuration for 100 residents & multiple board editors; 5) step-by-step protected-content implementation for Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events; 6) content update workflow for non-technical users; 7) backup/rollback/tests; 8) hand-off documentation. Break into clear numbered steps, note any placeholders, identify external dependencies, and provide roll-back instructions. Use STORE for lengthy artifacts. Request clarifications only if essential.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"DEP1\\\"\\n}\\n###o1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:12:49.317Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"o1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order DEP1 from agent 2: **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) – Dunbar Oaks HOA Website**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\nNOTE: Replace all `<PLACEHOLDER_…>` values (credentials, IDs, IPs, etc.) with real data at execution time. All commands assume macOS/Linux shell with sudo or equivalent IAM privileges.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\n0. Pre-Execution Summary\\\\\\\\n• Managed WP Host: **SiteGround “GrowBig”** (≈US$20/mo billed annually) – free SSL via Let’s Encrypt, daily backups, SG Security, staging, US-based data centers, GDPR-ready DPA.  \\\\\\\\n• Alt Option (commented): AWS Lightsail WordPress (US$5–10/mo) – include extra steps for snapshots & SSL via LetsEncrypt + Cron.  \\\\\\\\n• Residents (~100) View protected pages. Board Members (≈5–10) can edit.  \\\\\\\\n• Key Plugins: SG Optimizer, SG Security, Simple Membership, User Role Editor, WP Mail SMTP, UpdraftPlus, Contact Form 7, Redirection.\\\\\\\\n• Rollback tiers: (a) SiteGround auto daily backup, (b) UpdraftPlus off-site (S3/Google Drive), (c) manual MySQL+wp-content export before major changes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\n1. Provision Hosting & Domain\\\\\\\\n1.1 Purchase SiteGround “GrowBig” plan (if new) or create new site in existing account.  \\\\\\\\n1.2 Register dunbaroakshoa.com OR update registrar to custom DNS (SiteGround’s NS: `ns1.siteground.net`, `ns2.siteground.net`).  \\\\\\\\n1.3 Wait for propagation; verify with `dig dunbaroakshoa.com +short` resolves to SG IP.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. SSL & Basic Security\\\\\\\\n2.1 In SiteGround Site Tools → Security → SSL → “Let’s Encrypt”. Issue certificate for root + `www`.  \\\\\\\\n2.2 Enable “HTTPS Enforce” + HSTS in Site Tools.  \\\\\\\\n2.3 Turn on SG Security (firewall, login limiter, bot protection).  \\\\\\\\n2.4 Create SFTP user with limited perms `<sftp_hoa>` and strong key; disable password auth if desired.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. WordPress Installation\\\\\\\\n3.1 Site Tools → WordPress → Install & Manage → Install new WordPress.\\\\\\\\n    • Admin user: `<WP_ADMIN_USER>` (avoid ‘admin’).  \\\\\\\\n    • Email: `<admin@dunbaroakshoa.com>` routed via host or Google Workspace.\\\\\\\\n3.2 Record generated MySQL credentials securely (SiteGround auto‐creates DB).\\\\\\\\n3.3 Force HTTPS: SG Optimizer → Environment → “HTTPS Config” ➜ ON.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. WordPress Hardening\\\\\\\\n4.1 SG Security plugin → Hardenings: Disable XML-RPC, hide WP version, disable file editing.  \\\\\\\\n4.2 Edit `wp-config.php`:\\\\\\\\n    ```php\\\\\\\\n    define('DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT', true);\\\\\\\\n    define('WP_POST_REVISIONS', 5);\\\\\\\\n    define('AUTOSAVE_INTERVAL', 120);\\\\\\\\n    define('FORCE_SSL_ADMIN', true);\\\\\\\\n    define( 'WP_MEMORY_LIMIT', '256M' );\\\\\\\\n    ```\\\\\\\\n4.3 Change table prefix from default `wp_` during install (`hoa_` example).  \\\\\\\\n4.4 Limit login attempts (SG Security covers).  \\\\\\\\n4.5 Install Wordfence only if SG Security deemed insufficient (skip to reduce duplication).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. Theme & Child Theme\\\\\\\\n5.1 Install “GeneratePress” (free, lightweight, accessible).  \\\\\\\\n5.2 Create child theme:\\\\\\\\n    ```bash\\\\\\\\n    wp --allow-root scaffold child-theme dunbaroakshoa-child --parent_theme=generatepress --theme_name=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Dunbar Oaks HOA Child\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    ```\\\\\\\\n5.3 Add custom logo / colors later via Customizer; no branding exists now – use neutral palette (#004d40 teal accents, Sans-Serif fonts).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. Plugins – Install & Configure\\\\\\\\nUsing WP-CLI or WP Admin ➜ Plugins ➜ Add New.\\\\\\\\n6.1 **SG Optimizer** (auto-installed).  \\\\\\\\n6.2 **Simple Membership** – manage members, restrict pages.  \\\\\\\\n6.3 **User Role Editor** – create “Resident” (read), “Board” (edit_others_pages, edit_pages, upload_files).  \\\\\\\\n6.4 **WP Mail SMTP** – SMTP host: `<smtp.mailgun.org>` or SiteGround mail; set From address.  \\\\\\\\n6.5 **UpdraftPlus** – schedule daily backups to Google Drive bucket `<gdrive-folder-id>`.  \\\\\\\\n6.6 **Contact Form 7** – HOA contact form.  \\\\\\\\n6.7 **Redirection** – manage 301s if page structure changes.  \\\\\\\\n6.8 **Disable Comments** (optional).  \\\\\\\\n6.9 Activate & configure each.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. Membership & Role Setup\\\\\\\\n7.1 User Role Editor → Add role “Resident” (clone Subscriber).  \\\\\\\\n7.2 Add role “Board” (clone Editor, but remove `edit_theme_options`).\\\\\\\\n7.3 Simple Membership → Settings:\\\\\\\\n    • Enable WP user integration.  \\\\\\\\n    • Membership levels:\\\\\\\\n        – Resident (Level ID 2) ➜ Access to protected pages.  \\\\\\\\n        – Board (Level ID 3) ➜ Same as Resident + backend editing.\\\\\\\\n7.4 Registration: Disable public self-registration. Admin imports users.\\\\\\\\n7.5 Import Users:\\\\\\\\n    • Prepare CSV: email, first_name, last_name, address, membership_level_id.  \\\\\\\\n    • Use Simple Membership “Bulk Member Import” tool.\\\\\\\\n    • Residents receive activation email via SMTP.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n8. Protected Pages Implementation\\\\\\\\n8.1 Pages ➜ Add New pages:\\\\\\\\n    • Dues  \\\\\\\\n    • Annual Meetings  \\\\\\\\n    • News & Events\\\\\\\\n8.2 For each page → Simple Membership Protection meta-box ➜ check “Members only” (Resident + Board).  \\\\\\\\n8.3 Nav Menu: Appearance ➜ Menus ➜ Add above pages.  \\\\\\\\n    • Use Menu Visibility Plugin (optional) to hide menu items until logged-in.\\\\\\\\n8.4 Create landing page “Resident Login” with `/login` shortcode from Simple Membership.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n9. Content Update Workflow (Non-Technical)\\\\\\\\n9.1 Use Block Editor (Gutenberg). Provide quick‐edit doc (see Section 12).  \\\\\\\\n9.2 For News posts: categorize as “News & Events” category; create menu link to `/category/news-events`.\\\\\\\\n9.3 Board members edit pages: Pages ➜ select, click “Edit”, use blocks.\\\\\\\\n9.4 Media uploads via Media Library (max 2 MB, enforce via SG Optimizer settings).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n10. Email & SMTP\\\\\\\\n10.1 Create mailbox `noreply@dunbaroakshoa.com` in Site Tools ➜ Email.  \\\\\\\\n10.2 WP Mail SMTP ➜ Configure\\\\\\\\n    • Mailer: Other SMTP  \\\\\\\\n    • SMTP Host: `smtp.siteground.net`  \\\\\\\\n    • Encryption: TLS, Port 587  \\\\\\\\n    • Auth: yes, user/pass.  \\\\\\\\n10.3 Send test email.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n11. Backups & Rollback\\\\\\\\n11.1 SG automatic daily backup (retain 30 copies).  \\\\\\\\n11.2 UpdraftPlus to Google Drive – schedule daily, retain 15 copies.  \\\\\\\\n11.3 Manual snapshot before plugin/theme updates: Site Tools ➜ Backup ➜ Create.  \\\\\\\\nRollback Path:\\\\\\\\n    a) Minor WP error → SG Backup Restore to prior day.\\\\\\\\n    b) Major compromise → Provision clean SG instance, restore UpdraftPlus backup, rotate all creds.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n12. Hand-Off Documentation (Artifacts)\\\\\\\\n12.1 Create “HOA-Site-Admin-Guide.pdf” including:\\\\\\\\n    • Login URL & creds procedure\\\\\\\\n    • Adding/Removing residents\\\\\\\\n    • Posting news\\\\\\\\n    • Restoring from backups\\\\\\\\n12.2 Store file in `/wp-content/uploads/docs/` and share via Google Drive.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n13. GDPR/US Privacy Notes\\\\\\\\n13.1 Simple Membership stores PII (name, email, address). Enable Data Export/Erase in WP privacy settings.  \\\\\\\\n13.2 Add Privacy Policy page (SiteGround template) ➜ link in footer.  \\\\\\\\n13.3 Use reCAPTCHA on Contact Form 7.  \\\\\\\\n13.4 Honor unsubscribe & data deletion upon request (manual admin action).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n14. Testing Checklist\\\\\\\\n14.1 Anonymous visitor cannot access protected pages (expect redirect to login).  \\\\\\\\n14.2 Resident user logs in, sees pages.  \\\\\\\\n14.3 Board user can edit page, save, view update.  \\\\\\\\n14.4 Backup & Restore simulation in staging subdomain.  \\\\\\\\n14.5 Mobile responsiveness via BrowserStack.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n15. Go-Live\\\\\\\\n15.1 Enable SG Caching (Dynamic + Memcached).  \\\\\\\\n15.2 Switch “Search Engine Visibility” ➜ allow indexing.  \\\\\\\\n15.3 Announce launch via Mailgun campaign to residents.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n16. Maintenance Plan\\\\\\\\n16.1 Monthly: apply updates, test after.  \\\\\\\\n16.2 Quarterly: review user list, remove ex-residents.  \\\\\\\\n16.3 Annual: re-evaluate hosting cost vs usage; renew domain & SSL.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n17. Cost Estimate Summary\\\\\\\\n• SiteGround GrowBig: ~US$240 / yr (promo first yr ~US$120).  \\\\\\\\n• Domain: US$15 / yr.  \\\\\\\\n• UpdraftPlus (free) – optional Premium US$70 one-time.  \\\\\\\\n• Mailgun 10 k emails free/mo.  \\\\\\\\nTotal recurring ≈ US$255 / yr.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\nExecution Dependencies / Inputs Required\\\\\\\\n• SiteGround account credentials.  \\\\\\\\n• Registrar access (if separate).  \\\\\\\\n• GDrive or S3 creds for UpdraftPlus.  \\\\\\\\n• Resident CSV.  \\\\\\\\n• Board member emails.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\nEND DEP\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:12:49.317Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###sdep1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: STORE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"storageString\\\": \\\"DETERMINISTICALLY EXECUTABLE PLAN (DEP) – Dunbar Oaks HOA Website\\\\n\\\\nNOTE: Replace all <PLACEHOLDER_…> values (credentials, IDs, IPs, etc.) with real data at execution time. All commands assume macOS/Linux shell with sudo or equivalent IAM privileges.\\\\n\\\\n====================================================================\\\\n0. Pre-Execution Summary\\\\n• Managed WP Host: SiteGround “GrowBig” (≈US$20/mo billed annually) – free SSL via Let’s Encrypt, daily backups, SG Security, staging, US-based data centers, GDPR-ready DPA.\\\\n• Alt Option (commented): AWS Lightsail WordPress (US$5–10/mo) – include extra steps for snapshots & SSL via LetsEncrypt + Cron.\\\\n• Residents (~100) view protected pages. Board Members (≈5–10) can edit.\\\\n• Key Plugins: SG Optimizer, SG Security, Simple Membership, User Role Editor, WP Mail SMTP, UpdraftPlus, Contact Form 7, Redirection.\\\\n• Rollback tiers: (a) SiteGround auto daily backup, (b) UpdraftPlus off-site (S3/Google Drive), (c) manual MySQL+wp-content export before major changes.\\\\n\\\\n====================================================================\\\\n1. Provision Hosting & Domain\\\\n1.1 Purchase SiteGround “GrowBig” plan (if new) or create new site in existing account.\\\\n1.2 Register dunbaroakshoa.com OR update registrar to custom DNS (SiteGround’s NS: ns1.siteground.net, ns2.siteground.net).\\\\n1.3 Wait for propagation; verify with `dig dunbaroakshoa.com +short` resolves to SG IP.\\\\n\\\\n2. SSL & Basic Security\\\\n2.1 In SiteGround Site Tools → Security → SSL → “Let’s Encrypt”. Issue certificate for root + www.\\\\n2.2 Enable “HTTPS Enforce” + HSTS in Site Tools.\\\\n2.3 Turn on SG Security (firewall, login limiter, bot protection).\\\\n2.4 Create SFTP user with limited perms <sftp_hoa> and strong key; disable password auth if desired.\\\\n\\\\n3. WordPress Installation\\\\n3.1 Site Tools → WordPress → Install & Manage → Install new WordPress.\\\\n    • Admin user: <WP_ADMIN_USER> (avoid ‘admin’).\\\\n    • Email: <admin@dunbaroakshoa.com> routed via host or Google Workspace.\\\\n3.2 Record generated MySQL credentials securely (SiteGround auto-creates DB).\\\\n3.3 Force HTTPS: SG Optimizer → Environment → “HTTPS Config” ➜ ON.\\\\n\\\\n4. WordPress Hardening\\\\n4.1 SG Security plugin → Hardenings: Disable XML-RPC, hide WP version, disable file editing.\\\\n4.2 Edit wp-config.php:\\\\n    define('DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT', true);\\\\n    define('WP_POST_REVISIONS', 5);\\\\n    define('AUTOSAVE_INTERVAL', 120);\\\\n    define('FORCE_SSL_ADMIN', true);\\\\n    define('WP_MEMORY_LIMIT', '256M');\\\\n4.3 Change table prefix from default wp_ during install (hoa_ example).\\\\n4.4 Limit login attempts (SG Security covers).\\\\n4.5 Install Wordfence only if SG Security deemed insufficient (skip to reduce duplication).\\\\n\\\\n5. Theme & Child Theme\\\\n5.1 Install “GeneratePress” (free, lightweight, accessible).\\\\n5.2 Create child theme:\\\\n    wp --allow-root scaffold child-theme dunbaroakshoa-child --parent_theme=generatepress --theme_name=\\\\\\\"Dunbar Oaks HOA Child\\\\\\\"\\\\n5.3 Add custom logo / colors later via Customizer; no branding exists now – use neutral palette (#004d40 teal accents, Sans-Serif fonts).\\\\n\\\\n6. Plugins – Install & Configure\\\\n6.1 SG Optimizer (auto-installed).\\\\n6.2 Simple Membership – manage members, restrict pages.\\\\n6.3 User Role Editor – create “Resident” (read), “Board” (edit_others_pages, edit_pages, upload_files).\\\\n6.4 WP Mail SMTP – SMTP host: <smtp.mailgun.org> or SiteGround mail; set From address.\\\\n6.5 UpdraftPlus – schedule daily backups to Google Drive bucket <gdrive-folder-id>.\\\\n6.6 Contact Form 7 – HOA contact form.\\\\n6.7 Redirection – manage 301s if page structure changes.\\\\n6.8 Disable Comments (optional).\\\\n6.9 Activate & configure each.\\\\n\\\\n7. Membership & Role Setup\\\\n7.1 User Role Editor → Add role “Resident” (clone Subscriber).\\\\n7.2 Add role “Board” (clone Editor, but remove edit_theme_options).\\\\n7.3 Simple Membership → Settings:\\\\n    • Enable WP user integration.\\\\n    • Membership levels:\\\\n        – Resident (Level ID 2) ➜ Access to protected pages.\\\\n        – Board (Level ID 3) ➜ Same as Resident + backend editing.\\\\n7.4 Registration: Disable public self-registration. Admin imports users.\\\\n7.5 Import Users:\\\\n    • Prepare CSV: email, first_name, last_name, address, membership_level_id.\\\\n    • Use Simple Membership “Bulk Member Import” tool.\\\\n    • Residents receive activation email via SMTP.\\\\n\\\\n8. Protected Pages Implementation\\\\n8.1 Create pages: Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events.\\\\n8.2 For each page → Simple Membership Protection meta-box ➜ check “Members only” (Resident + Board).\\\\n8.3 Nav Menu: Appearance → Menus → Add above pages. Menu Visibility Plugin (optional) to hide menu items until logged-in.\\\\n8.4 Create landing page “Resident Login” with /login shortcode from Simple Membership.\\\\n\\\\n9. Content Update Workflow (Non-Technical)\\\\n9.1 Use Gutenberg Block Editor; provide quick-edit doc (see Section 12).\\\\n9.2 For News posts: categorize as “News & Events”; create menu link to /category/news-events.\\\\n9.3 Board members edit pages via Pages → Edit.\\\\n9.4 Media uploads via Media Library (max 2 MB; enforce via SG Optimizer).\\\\n\\\\n10. Email & SMTP\\\\n10.1 Create mailbox noreply@dunbaroakshoa.com in Site Tools → Email.\\\\n10.2 WP Mail SMTP → Configure mailer, host smtp.siteground.net, TLS 587.\\\\n10.3 Send test email.\\\\n\\\\n11. Backups & Rollback\\\\n11.1 SG automatic daily backup (retain 30 copies).\\\\n11.2 UpdraftPlus to Google Drive – schedule daily, retain 15 copies.\\\\n11.3 Manual snapshot before plugin/theme updates: Site Tools → Backup → Create.\\\\nRollback Path:\\\\n    a) Minor WP error → SG Backup Restore to prior day.\\\\n    b) Major compromise → Provision clean SG instance, restore UpdraftPlus backup, rotate all creds.\\\\n\\\\n12. Hand-Off Documentation\\\\n12.1 Create HOA-Site-Admin-Guide.pdf with login procedure, adding/removing residents, posting news, restoring backups.\\\\n12.2 Store PDF in /wp-content/uploads/docs/ and share via Google Drive.\\\\n\\\\n13. GDPR/US Privacy Notes\\\\n13.1 Simple Membership stores PII; enable Data Export/Erase in WP privacy settings.\\\\n13.2 Add Privacy Policy page; link in footer.\\\\n13.3 Use reCAPTCHA on Contact Form 7.\\\\n13.4 Honor unsubscribe & data deletion upon request.\\\\n\\\\n14. Testing Checklist\\\\n14.1 Anonymous visitor cannot access protected pages.\\\\n14.2 Resident user logs in, sees pages.\\\\n14.3 Board user can edit page, save, view update.\\\\n14.4 Backup & Restore simulation in staging.\\\\n14.5 Mobile responsiveness via BrowserStack.\\\\n\\\\n15. Go-Live\\\\n15.1 Enable SG Caching (Dynamic + Memcached).\\\\n15.2 Switch “Search Engine Visibility” → allow indexing.\\\\n15.3 Announce launch via Mailgun campaign to residents.\\\\n\\\\n16. Maintenance Plan\\\\n16.1 Monthly: apply updates, test.\\\\n16.2 Quarterly: review user list, remove ex-residents.\\\\n16.3 Annual: re-evaluate hosting cost; renew domain & SSL.\\\\n\\\\n17. Cost Estimate Summary\\\\n• SiteGround GrowBig: ~US$240 / yr (promo first yr ~US$120).\\\\n• Domain: US$15 / yr.\\\\n• UpdraftPlus (free) – optional Premium US$70 one-time.\\\\n• Mailgun 10 k emails free/mo.\\\\nTotal recurring ≈ US$255 / yr.\\\\n\\\\n====================================================================\\\\nExecution Dependencies / Inputs Required\\\\n• SiteGround account credentials.\\\\n• Registrar access (if separate).\\\\n• GDrive or S3 creds for UpdraftPlus.\\\\n• Resident CSV.\\\\n• Board member emails.\\\\n\\\\n====================================================================\\\\nEND DEP\\\"\\n}\\n###sdep1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:14:34.026Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"sdep1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Document successfully stored. Your unique storage ID is: DOC-000001\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:14:34.026Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###phase1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Comprehensive Deterministically Executable Plan for the Dunbar Oaks HOA website has been completed, reviewed, and stored. All required details—including hosting, security, protected content setup, workflow, backups, testing, and cost estimates—are covered. No additional clarifications are outstanding.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"DOC-000001\\\"\\n}\\n###phase1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:14:47.995Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"phase1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DENIED_BY_INTERNAL_REVIEW\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Phase shift was denied by internal review. Feedback from Partagaz D:\\\\\\\\nDENY  \\\\\\\\nThe DEP contains no substantive content beyond the placeholder “DOC-000001.” It does not address the user’s requirements, lacks all implementation details, and is neither deterministic nor testable.\\\\\\\\nDENY  \\\\\\\\nThe DEP contains no substantive content beyond an identifier (“DOC-000001”). It does not describe the system, include steps, code, dependencies, testing, or address any of the user’s requirements or clarification questions.\\\\\\\\nDENY: The DEP is empty (“DOC-000001” contains no plan). It provides none of the required deterministic steps, code, or details to meet the user’s needs, so it cannot be approved.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:14:47.995Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###rdep1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RETRIEVE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"retrievalString\\\": \\\"DOC-000001\\\"\\n}\\n###rdep1###\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":9107,\"outputTokens\":243,\"totalTokens\":9350},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-Bx0NEKa4ajIhpJc6Ei87EoBfytvFR\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1753402488,\"model\":\"o3-2025-04-16\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"###rdep1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RETRIEVE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"retrievalString\\\": \\\"DOC-000001\\\"\\n}\\n###rdep1###\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":9107,\"completion_tokens\":243,\"total_tokens\":9350,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":8704,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":192,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null},\"request\":{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"> **TL;DR for Agents:** Build the best solution with any appropriate tech stack. One call type per response. Use the Company File System (CFS) (STORE/RETRIEVE/FORGET) to keep context lean. Follow security, cost, and determinism principles. Ask only necessary clarifications. Deliver quality.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Core Principles\\n\\n1. **User-Centric Delivery:** The user's satisfaction and intent are paramount. Match or exceed requirements.\\n2. **Safety & Correctness First:** Validate assumptions, handle secrets carefully, and follow least-privilege access.\\n3. **Determinism & Traceability:** Plans should be executable step-by-step with minimal ambiguity. Log decisions.\\n4. **Efficiency:** Minimize cost, latency, and token usage (via CFS and concise messaging).\\n5. **Single Call Type Rule:** Exactly **one** system call type per response. Chain complex work across multiple turns.\\n6. **You are an AI Agent:** You operate within a deterministic system, not directly with the user. Your outputs are executed by the system, not by the user themselves. You do not mention times, ETAs, or deadlines, as these do not make sense in your paradigm. Your focus is on delivering the best solution for the user’s goals, regardless of the \\\"time\\\" it takes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert who can leverage **any suitable stack or platform**—AWS, Google Cloud, Azure, Vercel/Next.js, simple HTML/CSS/JS, on-prem tooling, etc.—to create robust, maintainable, and secure systems. You will:\\n\\n- Design and implement full-stack solutions end-to-end.\\n- Automate deployments and CI/CD where beneficial.\\n- Maintain security and compliance standards.\\n- Keep costs reasonable without sacrificing quality.\\n\\nYou collaborate within an AI-run development firm governed by a deterministic management system. Your outputs are read and executed by that system, not by the human user directly. Nevertheless, every action must serve the user’s goals.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. About the User & Collaboration Style\\n\\n- Assume full execution responsibility; do not offload tasks to the user unless required for missing information.\\n- Ask concise, necessary clarifications (via CLARIFY) when blocked or ambiguity risks failure.\\n- Be transparent about cost and security implications of your recommendations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Communication Model & System Messages\\n\\nYou operate in a closed loop: **system messages in, system calls out**. You never address the user directly.\\n\\n### System Message Types (Read-Only for Agents)\\n\\n```\\nSIM                – Kickoff message (Chief only)\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING – You sent no call\\nCALL_RESULTS       – Results of your executed call\\nORDERS             – Your superior's instructions\\nREPORTING          – Your report back to a superior’s order\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST   – Subordinate seeks your approval\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING – Your call was malformed\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING   – You issued new calls while old ones unresolved\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. System Calls\\n\\n**One call type per response.** Format every call exactly as shown.\\n\\n### Call Envelope\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n- `<UNIQUE_ID>` is any short unique tag.\\n- `<CALL_TYPE>` ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND, STORE, RETRIEVE, FORGET}.\\n- `<PAYLOAD_JSON>` must contain all required fields for that type.\\n\\n### Call Types & Required Fields\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY  { reasoning, questions[], options[] }  – Ask user for info (needs all superiors’ approval)\\nRECRUIT  { justification, title, customSystemInstructions } – Add a subordinate (must keep chain complete)\\nORDER    { orderString, recipientAgentID, orderSequenceID } – Instruct a direct report\\nREPORT   { reportString, originalOrderSequenceID } – Reply to an ORDER\\nPHASE    { justification, depString } – Move from Planning to Execution (Chief only)\\nCOMMAND  { justification, commandString } – Run CLI commands (Chief only, with authorization)\\nSTORE    { storageString } – Save a document to the CFS and drop from memory\\nRETRIEVE { retrievalString } – Load a stored document from the CFS into context\\nFORGET   { forgetString } – Drop a stored doc from your working memory (remains in CFS)\\n```\\n\\n> **CFS & Tokens:** STORE bulky docs to the CFS, RETRIEVE only when needed, FORGET after use. This keeps your prompt succinct and reduces token costs without losing access to artifacts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Phases of Work\\n\\n- **Planning Phase:** Analyze requirements, design solution, prepare a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). Seek approvals as needed.\\n- **Execution Phase:** Carry out the DEP through appropriate calls (mainly COMMAND/ORDER/REPORT chains).\\n- After execution, reassess, then iterate.\\n\\n### DEP Guidelines\\n\\n- Be step-by-step, minimal ambiguity.\\n- Include placeholders for unknown IDs or values, with instructions on how to obtain them.\\n- Note external dependencies and how to validate results.\\n- Account for rollbacks, cleanup, and testing.\\n- Must include ALL required code, steps, and commands to execute the plan fully.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Oversight & Quality Gates\\n\\n- **Partagaz D:** Reviews DEPs for completeness & determinism.\\n- **Partagaz C:** Approves COMMAND calls before execution.\\n- **Partagaz F:** Reviews documents sent to CFS for quality and standards.\\n\\nWhen you see an **APPROVAL\\\\_REQUEST**, respond with `$$$APPROVED$$$` to approve, or omit the string to deny.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Security, Cost, and Resource Management\\n\\n- Favor least-privilege IAM roles, secrets managers, and encrypted storage.\\n- Justify expensive resources. Prefer serverless or auto-scaling where appropriate.\\n- Clean up unused resources (add teardown steps to DEP).\\n- Redact or hash sensitive info if it must be stored.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Workload & Division of Labor\\n\\n- \\\"One file (or coherent unit of work) per agent at a time\\\" encourages focus.\\n- RECRUIT when specialization or parallelization is needed, then ORDER each recruit explicitly.\\n- REPORT promptly and thoroughly with the requested sequence ID.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Blank Responses, Malformed Calls & Runaways\\n\\n- A response without a call earns a BLANK\\\\_RESPONSE\\\\_WARNING. Fix and resend.\\n- Malformed calls halt all progress—validate format before submitting.\\n- Do not send new calls when a previous call is unresolved (avoid RUNAWAY\\\\_CALL\\\\_WARNING).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Quick Reference Templates\\n\\n### CLARIFY Example\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###c1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Need user’s preferred auth provider before designing login flow.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\\"Which auth provider do you prefer (Cognito, Firebase Auth, Auth0, custom)?\\\"],\\n  \\\"options\\\": [[\\\"Cognito\\\", \\\"Firebase\\\", \\\"Auth0\\\", \\\"Custom\\\", \\\"No preference\\\"]]\\n}\\n###c1###\\n```\\n\\n### STORE / RETRIEVE / FORGET Example\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###s42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: STORE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"storageString\\\": \\\"<long design doc text here>\\\"\\n}\\n###s42###\\n```\\n\\n*(Later)*\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###r42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RETRIEVE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"retrievalString\\\": \\\"<ID returned from STORE>\\\"\\n}\\n###r42###\\n```\\n\\n*(After use)*\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###f42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: FORGET\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"forgetString\\\": \\\"<same ID>\\\"\\n}\\n###f42###\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Final Reminder\\n\\n- Serve the user’s goal with rigor, safety, and efficiency.\\n- One call type per response.\\n- Use the CFS wisely to manage tokens.\\n- Be deterministic and transparent.\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\\nRemember to introduce yourself kindly, speak to the user as a real person might, and always be polite and professional. Your goal is to make the User feel comfortable and confident in your abilities as their Chief of Staff. For example, you might say something like:\\\\n\\\\nHello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. You can rely on me to help you stay organized, delegate tasks, and ensure that your objectives are met. What can I create for you today?\\\\n\\\\nYour initial Clarify should have only one question (like above) and should offer a single blank response for the User to fill in (no options). This will help you understand the User's current needs and how you can best assist them.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###c0###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Initial introduction and understanding the user's immediate needs will enable appropriate planning and resource allocation.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. What would you like assistance with today?\\\"],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###c0###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:09:57.786Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"c0\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. What would you like assistance with today?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:09:57.786Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###c1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"To design an HOA website that meets usability, security, and maintenance expectations, I need to confirm the preferred technology stack, branding assets, and hosting details.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1) Do you have any preference for the platform (e.g., WordPress with a membership plugin, Squarespace, Wix, or a custom-built site)?\\\",\\n    \\\"2) Do you already own a domain name and/or hosting account, or would you like me to arrange that?\\\",\\n    \\\"3) Are there any existing logos, color schemes, or design inspirations you’d like incorporated?\\\",\\n    \\\"4) Roughly how many residents will need accounts for the restricted areas so we can size the solution appropriately?\\\",\\n    \\\"5) Will you be the primary person updating news & events, or will multiple board members need editing access?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###c1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:10:43.916Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"1) Do you have any preference for the platform (e.g., WordPress with a membership plugin, Squarespace, Wix, or a custom-built site)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I don't know what any of those are\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"2) Do you already own a domain name and/or hosting account, or would you like me to arrange that?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"3) Are there any existing logos, color schemes, or design inspirations you’d like incorporated?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"4) Roughly how many residents will need accounts for the restricted areas so we can size the solution appropriately?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"100\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"5) Will you be the primary person updating news & events, or will multiple board members need editing access?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Multiple board members\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:10:43.916Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###r1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"We need an experienced leader to architect and oversee the build-out of a user-friendly, secure HOA website (≈100 resident accounts, multiple board editors). The role requires deep WordPress and membership-site expertise to craft a deterministic execution plan and subsequent implementation orders.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of HOA Website Development\\\",\\n  \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\": \\\"You will design and later oversee implementation of a WordPress-based HOA site for dunbaroakshoa.com with protected pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events) accessible to logged-in residents (≈100). Requirements: \\\\n• Choose cost-effective managed WordPress hosting with SSL (e.g., SiteGround, Lightsail, or similar).\\\\n• Select a lightweight, accessible theme and necessary plugins: membership (e.g., Simple Membership), contact form, role editor, backups, SMTP, security hardening.\\\\n• Define resident and board roles; board members can edit content while residents view protected pages.\\\\n• Provide non-technical update workflow (block editor or page-builder, clear instructions).\\\\n• Outline page structure, navigation, basic styling guidance (no existing branding).\\\\n• Include DNS steps for pointing dunbaroakshoa.com to host.\\\\n• Deliver a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) covering provisioning, WordPress install, plugin/theme setup, security configuration, content migration placeholders, user import, testing, and hand-off docs.\\\\n• Incorporate rollback/backup strategy and cost estimate.\\\\n• Adhere to least-privilege principles and mention GDPR/US privacy considerations.\\\\nOutput: DEP as a clear numbered list; store lengthy artifacts to CFS via STORE; request clarifications only if essential.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###r1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:11:45.777Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"r1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Motti (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:11:45.777Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###o1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please draft a comprehensive Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for building the HOA website per your recruiting brief. Include: 1) hosting/provider selection with cost/security rationale; 2) DNS and SSL setup for dunbaroakshoa.com; 3) WordPress installation and hardening steps; 4) theme + plugin list with setup/role configuration for 100 residents & multiple board editors; 5) step-by-step protected-content implementation for Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events; 6) content update workflow for non-technical users; 7) backup/rollback/tests; 8) hand-off documentation. Break into clear numbered steps, note any placeholders, identify external dependencies, and provide roll-back instructions. Use STORE for lengthy artifacts. Request clarifications only if essential.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"DEP1\\\"\\n}\\n###o1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:12:49.317Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"o1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order DEP1 from agent 2: **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) – Dunbar Oaks HOA Website**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\nNOTE: Replace all `<PLACEHOLDER_…>` values (credentials, IDs, IPs, etc.) with real data at execution time. All commands assume macOS/Linux shell with sudo or equivalent IAM privileges.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\n0. Pre-Execution Summary\\\\\\\\n• Managed WP Host: **SiteGround “GrowBig”** (≈US$20/mo billed annually) – free SSL via Let’s Encrypt, daily backups, SG Security, staging, US-based data centers, GDPR-ready DPA.  \\\\\\\\n• Alt Option (commented): AWS Lightsail WordPress (US$5–10/mo) – include extra steps for snapshots & SSL via LetsEncrypt + Cron.  \\\\\\\\n• Residents (~100) View protected pages. Board Members (≈5–10) can edit.  \\\\\\\\n• Key Plugins: SG Optimizer, SG Security, Simple Membership, User Role Editor, WP Mail SMTP, UpdraftPlus, Contact Form 7, Redirection.\\\\\\\\n• Rollback tiers: (a) SiteGround auto daily backup, (b) UpdraftPlus off-site (S3/Google Drive), (c) manual MySQL+wp-content export before major changes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\n1. Provision Hosting & Domain\\\\\\\\n1.1 Purchase SiteGround “GrowBig” plan (if new) or create new site in existing account.  \\\\\\\\n1.2 Register dunbaroakshoa.com OR update registrar to custom DNS (SiteGround’s NS: `ns1.siteground.net`, `ns2.siteground.net`).  \\\\\\\\n1.3 Wait for propagation; verify with `dig dunbaroakshoa.com +short` resolves to SG IP.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. SSL & Basic Security\\\\\\\\n2.1 In SiteGround Site Tools → Security → SSL → “Let’s Encrypt”. Issue certificate for root + `www`.  \\\\\\\\n2.2 Enable “HTTPS Enforce” + HSTS in Site Tools.  \\\\\\\\n2.3 Turn on SG Security (firewall, login limiter, bot protection).  \\\\\\\\n2.4 Create SFTP user with limited perms `<sftp_hoa>` and strong key; disable password auth if desired.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. WordPress Installation\\\\\\\\n3.1 Site Tools → WordPress → Install & Manage → Install new WordPress.\\\\\\\\n    • Admin user: `<WP_ADMIN_USER>` (avoid ‘admin’).  \\\\\\\\n    • Email: `<admin@dunbaroakshoa.com>` routed via host or Google Workspace.\\\\\\\\n3.2 Record generated MySQL credentials securely (SiteGround auto‐creates DB).\\\\\\\\n3.3 Force HTTPS: SG Optimizer → Environment → “HTTPS Config” ➜ ON.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. WordPress Hardening\\\\\\\\n4.1 SG Security plugin → Hardenings: Disable XML-RPC, hide WP version, disable file editing.  \\\\\\\\n4.2 Edit `wp-config.php`:\\\\\\\\n    ```php\\\\\\\\n    define('DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT', true);\\\\\\\\n    define('WP_POST_REVISIONS', 5);\\\\\\\\n    define('AUTOSAVE_INTERVAL', 120);\\\\\\\\n    define('FORCE_SSL_ADMIN', true);\\\\\\\\n    define( 'WP_MEMORY_LIMIT', '256M' );\\\\\\\\n    ```\\\\\\\\n4.3 Change table prefix from default `wp_` during install (`hoa_` example).  \\\\\\\\n4.4 Limit login attempts (SG Security covers).  \\\\\\\\n4.5 Install Wordfence only if SG Security deemed insufficient (skip to reduce duplication).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. Theme & Child Theme\\\\\\\\n5.1 Install “GeneratePress” (free, lightweight, accessible).  \\\\\\\\n5.2 Create child theme:\\\\\\\\n    ```bash\\\\\\\\n    wp --allow-root scaffold child-theme dunbaroakshoa-child --parent_theme=generatepress --theme_name=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Dunbar Oaks HOA Child\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    ```\\\\\\\\n5.3 Add custom logo / colors later via Customizer; no branding exists now – use neutral palette (#004d40 teal accents, Sans-Serif fonts).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. Plugins – Install & Configure\\\\\\\\nUsing WP-CLI or WP Admin ➜ Plugins ➜ Add New.\\\\\\\\n6.1 **SG Optimizer** (auto-installed).  \\\\\\\\n6.2 **Simple Membership** – manage members, restrict pages.  \\\\\\\\n6.3 **User Role Editor** – create “Resident” (read), “Board” (edit_others_pages, edit_pages, upload_files).  \\\\\\\\n6.4 **WP Mail SMTP** – SMTP host: `<smtp.mailgun.org>` or SiteGround mail; set From address.  \\\\\\\\n6.5 **UpdraftPlus** – schedule daily backups to Google Drive bucket `<gdrive-folder-id>`.  \\\\\\\\n6.6 **Contact Form 7** – HOA contact form.  \\\\\\\\n6.7 **Redirection** – manage 301s if page structure changes.  \\\\\\\\n6.8 **Disable Comments** (optional).  \\\\\\\\n6.9 Activate & configure each.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. Membership & Role Setup\\\\\\\\n7.1 User Role Editor → Add role “Resident” (clone Subscriber).  \\\\\\\\n7.2 Add role “Board” (clone Editor, but remove `edit_theme_options`).\\\\\\\\n7.3 Simple Membership → Settings:\\\\\\\\n    • Enable WP user integration.  \\\\\\\\n    • Membership levels:\\\\\\\\n        – Resident (Level ID 2) ➜ Access to protected pages.  \\\\\\\\n        – Board (Level ID 3) ➜ Same as Resident + backend editing.\\\\\\\\n7.4 Registration: Disable public self-registration. Admin imports users.\\\\\\\\n7.5 Import Users:\\\\\\\\n    • Prepare CSV: email, first_name, last_name, address, membership_level_id.  \\\\\\\\n    • Use Simple Membership “Bulk Member Import” tool.\\\\\\\\n    • Residents receive activation email via SMTP.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n8. Protected Pages Implementation\\\\\\\\n8.1 Pages ➜ Add New pages:\\\\\\\\n    • Dues  \\\\\\\\n    • Annual Meetings  \\\\\\\\n    • News & Events\\\\\\\\n8.2 For each page → Simple Membership Protection meta-box ➜ check “Members only” (Resident + Board).  \\\\\\\\n8.3 Nav Menu: Appearance ➜ Menus ➜ Add above pages.  \\\\\\\\n    • Use Menu Visibility Plugin (optional) to hide menu items until logged-in.\\\\\\\\n8.4 Create landing page “Resident Login” with `/login` shortcode from Simple Membership.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n9. Content Update Workflow (Non-Technical)\\\\\\\\n9.1 Use Block Editor (Gutenberg). Provide quick‐edit doc (see Section 12).  \\\\\\\\n9.2 For News posts: categorize as “News & Events” category; create menu link to `/category/news-events`.\\\\\\\\n9.3 Board members edit pages: Pages ➜ select, click “Edit”, use blocks.\\\\\\\\n9.4 Media uploads via Media Library (max 2 MB, enforce via SG Optimizer settings).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n10. Email & SMTP\\\\\\\\n10.1 Create mailbox `noreply@dunbaroakshoa.com` in Site Tools ➜ Email.  \\\\\\\\n10.2 WP Mail SMTP ➜ Configure\\\\\\\\n    • Mailer: Other SMTP  \\\\\\\\n    • SMTP Host: `smtp.siteground.net`  \\\\\\\\n    • Encryption: TLS, Port 587  \\\\\\\\n    • Auth: yes, user/pass.  \\\\\\\\n10.3 Send test email.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n11. Backups & Rollback\\\\\\\\n11.1 SG automatic daily backup (retain 30 copies).  \\\\\\\\n11.2 UpdraftPlus to Google Drive – schedule daily, retain 15 copies.  \\\\\\\\n11.3 Manual snapshot before plugin/theme updates: Site Tools ➜ Backup ➜ Create.  \\\\\\\\nRollback Path:\\\\\\\\n    a) Minor WP error → SG Backup Restore to prior day.\\\\\\\\n    b) Major compromise → Provision clean SG instance, restore UpdraftPlus backup, rotate all creds.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n12. Hand-Off Documentation (Artifacts)\\\\\\\\n12.1 Create “HOA-Site-Admin-Guide.pdf” including:\\\\\\\\n    • Login URL & creds procedure\\\\\\\\n    • Adding/Removing residents\\\\\\\\n    • Posting news\\\\\\\\n    • Restoring from backups\\\\\\\\n12.2 Store file in `/wp-content/uploads/docs/` and share via Google Drive.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n13. GDPR/US Privacy Notes\\\\\\\\n13.1 Simple Membership stores PII (name, email, address). Enable Data Export/Erase in WP privacy settings.  \\\\\\\\n13.2 Add Privacy Policy page (SiteGround template) ➜ link in footer.  \\\\\\\\n13.3 Use reCAPTCHA on Contact Form 7.  \\\\\\\\n13.4 Honor unsubscribe & data deletion upon request (manual admin action).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n14. Testing Checklist\\\\\\\\n14.1 Anonymous visitor cannot access protected pages (expect redirect to login).  \\\\\\\\n14.2 Resident user logs in, sees pages.  \\\\\\\\n14.3 Board user can edit page, save, view update.  \\\\\\\\n14.4 Backup & Restore simulation in staging subdomain.  \\\\\\\\n14.5 Mobile responsiveness via BrowserStack.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n15. Go-Live\\\\\\\\n15.1 Enable SG Caching (Dynamic + Memcached).  \\\\\\\\n15.2 Switch “Search Engine Visibility” ➜ allow indexing.  \\\\\\\\n15.3 Announce launch via Mailgun campaign to residents.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n16. Maintenance Plan\\\\\\\\n16.1 Monthly: apply updates, test after.  \\\\\\\\n16.2 Quarterly: review user list, remove ex-residents.  \\\\\\\\n16.3 Annual: re-evaluate hosting cost vs usage; renew domain & SSL.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n17. Cost Estimate Summary\\\\\\\\n• SiteGround GrowBig: ~US$240 / yr (promo first yr ~US$120).  \\\\\\\\n• Domain: US$15 / yr.  \\\\\\\\n• UpdraftPlus (free) – optional Premium US$70 one-time.  \\\\\\\\n• Mailgun 10 k emails free/mo.  \\\\\\\\nTotal recurring ≈ US$255 / yr.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\nExecution Dependencies / Inputs Required\\\\\\\\n• SiteGround account credentials.  \\\\\\\\n• Registrar access (if separate).  \\\\\\\\n• GDrive or S3 creds for UpdraftPlus.  \\\\\\\\n• Resident CSV.  \\\\\\\\n• Board member emails.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n====================================================================\\\\\\\\nEND DEP\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULT